1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,750
You're looking at Britain's top general,

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,420
days before D-Day. It's a pay clerk.

3
00:00:04,990 --> 00:00:06,760
Why would Britain fake its own general?

4
00:00:07,221 --> 00:00:09,431
Britain wanted German eyes on the Mediterranean,

5
00:00:10,061 --> 00:00:12,741
not Normandy. So it borrowed Montgomery's

6
00:00:12,741 --> 00:00:13,131
face.

7
00:00:13,525 --> 00:00:15,595
Lieutenant Clifton James was an actor,

8
00:00:15,945 --> 00:00:18,135
stuck counting money in the Army Pay Corps.

9
00:00:18,725 --> 00:00:20,845
Then a newspaper photo showed he was Monty's

10
00:00:20,845 --> 00:00:21,195
twin.

11
00:00:21,561 --> 00:00:23,941
There were problems. Monty never drank or

12
00:00:23,941 --> 00:00:25,951
smoked. James did both.

13
00:00:26,341 --> 00:00:28,021
And he'd lost a finger in the First World

14
00:00:28,021 --> 00:00:29,811
War, so they made him a fake one.

15
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:31,962
He studied the real Monty up close,

16
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:33,482
posing as a reporter,

17
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:35,362
learning his walk and his voice.

18
00:00:35,741 --> 00:00:38,381
In late May, he flew to Gibraltar on Churchill's

19
00:00:38,381 --> 00:00:41,101
own plane. Reportedly, it circled for an

20
00:00:41,101 --> 00:00:43,321
hour, so he could sober up from smuggled

21
00:00:43,321 --> 00:00:43,831
gin.

22
00:00:44,251 --> 00:00:45,991
At breakfast, the governor talked about

23
00:00:45,991 --> 00:00:48,591
secret plans, in front of a Spanish visitor

24
00:00:48,591 --> 00:00:50,121
known to spy for Germany.

25
00:00:50,851 --> 00:00:52,501
He crossed the border to call his handler.

26
00:00:52,899 --> 00:00:54,679
Then Algiers. Crowds, cameras,

27
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:56,289
a meeting with General Wilson.

28
00:00:57,079 --> 00:00:57,949
Then the double vanished,

29
00:00:58,159 --> 00:01:00,016
hidden in Cairo until D-Day.

30
00:01:00,126 --> 00:01:02,526
Did it work? Captured German generals said

31
00:01:02,526 --> 00:01:03,996
they believed it was Monty,

32
00:01:04,206 --> 00:01:05,276
but guessed it was a trick.

33
00:01:05,846 --> 00:01:07,986
Historians find no sign it changed their

34
00:01:07,986 --> 00:01:08,436
plans.

35
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,400
James got £10 a day,

36
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,530
Monty's pay, then went back to his desk.

37
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,170
Genius, or a waste?

38
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,630
Tell me below, and follow Buried Chronicles.

